    "title": "Boston Marathon 2026 is almost here. Route, start time, how to watch",
    "text": "April 19, 2026, 2:00 p.m. ETTens of thousands of runners are getting ready to lace up for the 130th Boston Marathon.Every year, runners flock to Massachusetts from all around the globe to hit the course of the long-running race, while thousands of others line the route to cheer them on.One of seven World Marathon Majors, the Boston Marathon falls each year on Patriots' Day, a Massachusetts holiday commemorating the battles of Lexington and Concord.The race begins west of Boston in the town of Hopkinton before leading runners through several more cities then concluding in Boston's Back Bay neighborhood.Here's what to know about this year's Boston Marathon, including how to watch from home.When is the Boston Marathon?The Boston Marathon is on Monday, April 20 this year.How to watch the Boston MarathonThe Boston Marathon will be broadcast nationwide on ESPN2 from 9 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. ET on April 20.Some race coverage will also air on ESPN throughout the day.Those in the New England area can also watch live coverage beginning at 4 a.m. ET on their local ABC affiliate station, including WCVB Channel 5, WMUR News 9 (Manchester, New Hampshire), WMTW Channel 8 (Portland, Maine) and WPTZ NBC5 (Burlington, Vermont/Plattsburgh, New York).Watch the Boston Marathon on ESPN2 with Fubo hereWhat time does the Boston Marathon start?The Boston Marathon begins in waves to stagger runners on the course.See the start times by category:Wheelchair Men - 9:06 a.m.Wheelchair Women - 9:09 a.m.Handcycles/Duos - 9:30 a.m.Professional Men - 9:37 a.m.Professional Women - 9:47 a.m.Para Athletics Division - 9:50 a.m.Wave 1 - 10:00 a.m.Wave 2 - 10:15 a.m.Wave 3 - 10:28 a.m.Wave 4 - 10:41 a.m.Wave 5 - 11:01 a.m.Wave 6 - 11:21 a.m.How many people run the Boston Marathon?More than 30,000 people from nearly 130 countries and all 50 states are expected to participate in the 130th Boston Marathon, according to organizers.Each of the six main starting waves will range in size from 3,200 to 7,100 athletes, according to the Boston Athletic Association.They will have an army of supporters: The BAA estimates that more than 500,000 spectators will line the route.Boston Marathon course mapThe Boston Marathon start line is located in Hopkinton, which is west of the city.Runners traverse roads in towns and cities, including Ashland, Framingham, Natick, Wellesley, Newton and Brookline, before making their way to Boston.The finish line is located on Boylston Street in Boston.See the full course map on BAA's website.Melina Khan is a national trending reporter for USA TODAY. Keep up with her on X @melinakh and Instagram @bymelinakhan.",
